nuating circumstances, e.g., when you request that the applicant submit a birth certificate instead of a notification of birth registration, and the applicant insists that the notification of birth registration is the birth certificate; and\",\"meaning_assertion_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:8c25a4632fe5a07d3e1433437159aef42d76f36a3dc0d2eacd302533509d5466\",\"modality\":\"must_not\",\"modality_quote\":\"must not\",\"object\":\"\",\"occurrence_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:occurrence:cfced9d9355fa9fca613661c4a660be6667a2a2a2ab00a710d9f626724ba0114\",\"origin\":\"aiSuggested\",\"quote\":\"(1) Passport agencies/centers must not make unilateral changes or alterations to the IRLs without the approval of the Office of Adjudication (CA/PPT/S/A) except on a case-by-case basis with the approval of passport agency/center management in extenuating circumstances, e.g., when you request that the applicant submit a birth certificate instead of a notification of birth registration, and the applicant insists that the notification of birth registration is the birth certificate; and\",\"references\":[\"CA/PPT/S/A\"],\"relation\":\"none\",\"rule_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:rule:0c924a19144af8ced124923d466c80c9b0465cab8c03599f2fad64be54089d59\",\"scope_quotes\":[\"(1) Passport agencies/centers must not make unilateral changes or alterations to the IRLs without the approval of the Office of Adjudication (CA/PPT/S/A) except on a case-by-case basis with the approval of passport agency/center management in extenuating circumstances, e.g., when you request that the applicant submit a birth certificate instead of a notification of birth registration, and the applicant insists that the notification of birth registration is the birth certificate; and\"],\"scope_text\":\"Passport agencies/centers making changes or alterations to IRLs without the approval of the Office of Adjudication (CA/PPT/S/A), except on a case-by-case basis with the approval of passport agency/center management in extenuating circumstances\",\"section_id\":\"section-1\",\"start\":653,\"summary\":\"Passport agencies/centers must not make unilateral changes or alterations to the IRLs without the approval of the Office of Adjudication (CA/PPT/S/A) except on a case-by-case basis with the approval of passport agency/center management in extenuating circumstances (e.g., when requesting that the applicant submit a birth certificate instead of a notification of birth registration, and the applicant insists that the notification of birth registration is the birth certificate).\",\"target_ids\":[],\"typed_values\":[]}",
